.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- remove files using colon-path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I FILE
\&...
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
wraps
.BR rm (1).
Each
.B BASE:LEAF
argument is rewritten to the physical path
.B BASE/LEAF .
.PP
After a colon-path file (or tree) is removed, empty parent directories along
.I LEAF
are removed with
.BR rmdir (2)
when possible.
.B BASE
itself is never removed.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ .:d/e/f
Removes file
.BR d/e/f ,
then tries
.B rmdir d/e
and
.B rmdir d
if those directories are empty.
.TP
.B @COLON@ \-rf a/b:c/d
Runs
.B rm \-rf a/b/c/d ,
then prunes empty parents under
.B a/b
along
.BR c/d .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the planned
.B rm
and parent
.B rmdir
steps without executing them.
.PP
Other options are passed through to
.BR rm (1).
See the original manual for the complete option set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rm (1),
.BR colon-rmdir (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
